// Soester Boerde — 5 km across real farmland east of Soest, and the module the
// field, road and DGM imports are demonstrated on. Everything but the `fields:`,
// `roads:` and `heights:` data is a few lines of track: what makes it worth
// driving is that the countryside beside it — its crops, its roads and its
// ground — is the countryside that is actually there.
//
//   cargo run -p app -- --scenario example:boerdefahrt
//
// The fields came from the Landwirtschaftskammer Nordrhein-Westfalen's InVeKoS
// service for the 2026 application year (dl-de/by-2-0, see `field_sources:` and
// THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md). The roads came from OpenStreetMap (ODbL): 531
// carriageways, motorway to Feldweg, the centre lines the mappers surveyed —
// the field tracks among them unpaved unless a mapper wrote otherwise, which
// is what the Boerde is stitched with. The ground came from NRW's open-data
// DGM1 (GeoTIFF, (C) Geobasis NRW, dl-de/by-2-0): the corridor's terrain tiles
// are cut at 10 m spacing into `heights/boerde/` and the line records them, so
// the module runs without `--dgm`. The track stands where the ground is —
// 92.4 m NHN at the start, over the dip at km 2, up to 103.5 m at the east
// end, the grades fitted to the DGM in half-kilometre nodes.
//
// Everything here is re-fetchable in one go, headless — the fields out of the
// register, the roads out of Overpass, the DGM sheets out of NRW's open data
// and the track onto them:
//
//   cargo run -p content --bin import-module -- \
//       --line mods/example/lines/boerde.ron --tracks \
//       --dgm cache/dgm/nrw --fetch-dgm nrw
//
// `--tracks` is what brings the Wirtschaftswege in (and, with them, the service
// roads of the yards — the flag opts both of the many-and-thin classes in).
//
// The route editor does the same three imports by dialog: File > Import fields,
// File > Import roads, and the Height data (DGM) panel for the cut-out.
//
// 134 fields, 676 ha. Crops as of the import:
//    winter-cereal 63
//           maize 21
//       grassland 16
//          potato 11
//      sugar-beet 10
//        rapeseed  5
//          legume  4
//  summer-cereal  1
//       vegetable  1
//         orchard  1
//          fallow  1
//
// 531 roads, 72.9 km of centre line, as of the import:
//    service 191       residential 133   secondary 58   tertiary 57
//    unclassified 37   track 33          primary 11     trunk 7
//    secondary_link 2  tertiary_link 2
//
// By surface: 478 asphalt, 30 concrete, 23 gravel. Of the 33 field tracks,
// 21 are gravel — the 11 asphalt and the one concrete slab among them say so
// themselves (`surface=*`, `tracktype=grade1`). Nothing unpaved carries a
// marking.
